condition_name: Temporomandibular Joint Pain Dysfunction Syndrome
condition_slug: temporomandibular_joint_pain_dysfunction_syndrome
source: NSTG 2022
introduction: The most common problem in or around the TMJ.
clinical_features[2]:
  - type: Demographics
    features[2]: "Equal frequency between genders, but five times as many females seek treatment",Patients are usually between 15 and 40 years
  - type: Symptoms
    features[6]: "Unilateral or bilateral dull pain within the TMJ and/or surrounding muscles, sometimes on waking or during eating or speech","TMJ may lock in the open or closed positions, occasionally","TMJ sounds such as clicking, crunching or grating",Associated headache is usually located in the temporal region,"Pain is cyclical and usually resolves, but may recur",May be associated with psychological stress
investigations[0]:
treatment:
  goals[1]: Conservative and reversible treatment
  non_drug[5]: Most symptoms are self-limiting and do not require treatment,"Educate patient about the condition, emphasizing its frequency and self-limiting nature",Soft diet,Apply moist heat to painful muscles,Physiotherapy
  drug[3]: Analgesics as appropriate,Anxiolytics,"Diazepam 5 mg orally 1 hour before sleep, then 2.5 mg every 12 hours, for up to 10 days (maximum)"
  adverse_reactions_and_cautions[0]:
  supportive_measures[1]: Occlusal splints
differential_diagnoses[2]: Migraine,Psychologic depression
complications[0]:
prevention[0]:
other_investigations: null
definitive_treatment: null
prognosis: null